────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEFECT 3 — `trip_drives` is a valid post-phase-42 SI table, not legacy
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The bannedTables list inside this prompt's gate includes `trip_drives`,
but `trip_drives` is RECREATED as a first-class SI table by 000172:

  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:81  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS trip_drives CASCADE;
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:217 CREATE TABLE trip_drives (
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:218   trip_id  BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES trips(id)  ON DELETE CASCADE,
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:219   drive_id BIGINT NOT NULL REFERENCES drives(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:220   position INT    NOT NULL,
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:222   PRIMARY KEY (trip_id, drive_id)
  migrations/000172_drives_si.up.sql:223 );

Phase-42 prompt 0076 (HEAD fea5c887, STATUS=DONE) explicitly added
`SELECT/INSERT/JOIN trip_drives` in trip_repo.go to expose the SI
schema's user-curated trip composition (M:N join with `position` for
ordering, totals derived from drives via JOIN — see
phase-42-0076-consumer-positions-trips.log § STRATEGY_DECISION
"trips/drives column eliminations").

`trip_drives` belongs in the SAME category as the post-SI `drives`,
`charging_sessions`, `positions`, `trips`, and `signal_log` tables —
all of which are recreated by 000169-000175 and are in active use by
post-phase-42 code. None of those other recreated tables are in the
bannedTables list. Including `trip_drives` is a copy-paste defect in
the gate.

The fix is in the gate, not the consumer code: `trip_drives` should be
removed from the bannedTables array in this prompt's gate. The
trip_repo.go references are correct under ADR-004 #4 and must be
preserved.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SUMMARY: gate-vs-spec contradiction
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The prompt's spec text correctly identifies the work that needs to
happen (rewrite cross-domain analytics + delete the four orphan-table
repos + remove deleted-handler routes from router.go). The strategy
table is sound. The deletion list is sound.

The defect is in the gate's two narrowing controls:

  (i) allowedRegex limits modifications to 13 files. To zero out the
      bannedTables grep (the gate's stated success condition) we must
      modify ~17 additional unallowed files — either to delete handler
      files for the orphan-only features (vampire_drain_handler.go,
      mileage_handler.go, vehicle_state_handler.go), or to rewrite
      retained-feature handlers/repos that still query dropped tables
      (temp_impact_handler.go, signal_observation_repo.go,
      signal_catalog_repo.go, telemetry_handler.go, battery_handler.go,
      analytics_handler_queries.go, export/analytics.go,
      signal_history_writer.go, regen_handler.go, energy_repo.go,
      security_repo.go, fsm_handler.go, telemetry_handler_wiring.go,
      vehicle_service.go, port/repository/vehicle.go, guard_handler.go),
      AND drop the route wiring for guard_handler if guard becomes
      orphan-only.

  (ii) bannedTables incorrectly includes `trip_drives`, a valid
       post-phase-42 SI table created by 000172. Even with no other
       changes, the existing trip_repo.go references from STATUS=DONE
       prompt 0076 trip the check (4 hits).

This pattern matches the phase-42-0078-mig-drop-legacy.log § BLOCKED_SUMMARY:
the consumer-migration prompts (0060-0072 + 0073-0076) each migrate
narrow allowed-files slices and explicitly defer related read-handler /
repo migrations to follow-on prompts that were never fully authored —
0077 was supposed to be that follow-on, but its allowed-files list is
~17 files short of the actual surface area required.

